          "body": "Rebased on `develop` and reworked to match the review: the tooltip now lives on the palette bricks, not on every brick in the workspace.\n\n## What this does\n\nHovering or focusing a brick in the palette reveals its tooltip after a short delay. The slot showed its entry's `description` through a native `title`; that is now the delayed tooltip, preferring the brick's own `tooltipText` and falling back to the description. Keeping both would have stacked a native tooltip on top of this one.\n\n- `hooks/useBrickTooltip.ts` — the hover delay (500 ms), cancellation, drag suppression and timer cleanup.\n- `components/Palette/BrickTooltip.tsx` — the tooltip itself: rendered into `document.body`, positioned from the slot's client rect, flipping below when there is no room above, wrapping at 256px and clamped to the window.\n- `components/Palette/BrickSlot.tsx` — pointer and focus handlers, and the `title` it replaces.\n\nFocus opens it as well as hover, so the text is not pointer only.\n\n## Following the review\n\nPer @parthdagia05 and @kh-ub-ayb above, hover tooltips are palette-only; `BrickFixed` and `BrickInput` are back to how `develop` has them. The pie menu `?` for workspace bricks is not in this PR — I have asked below how it should present the text before building it.\n\nTwo things worth settling:\n\n- **This may belong to #685** (\"Show tooltip when hovering over Bricks in the Palette\") rather than #843, now that the workspace half has moved to the pie menu. Happy to retarget.\n- **The drag suppression watches the pointer button**, not `dragStateAtom`. `recoil@0.7.7` does not work with `react@19` — `useRecoilValue` destructures `react.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED`, which React 19 removed, so it throws on render. The first version of this used the atom and failed every brick test with it. Worth knowing separately: `WorkspaceView.tsx:33` calls `useRecoilValue(dragStateAtom)` and has no test, so that is live and uncaught.\n\n## Why the tooltip renders in a portal\n\nDrawing it inside the brick's `<svg>` passed the tests but broke two things in a browser:\n\n1. **It widened the brick's bounding box** — `getBBox()` on a hovered brick reported `10003x71` instead of `103x30`, and the workspace measures brick geometry for canvas bounds and auto scroll.\n2. **An ancestor hiding its overflow clipped it** — measured top `-24px` against a container starting at `0`.\n\nBoth matter doubly in the palette, whose panel scrolls and clips. Measured after the change: `getBBox()` is unchanged with a tooltip open, and the tooltip escapes the panel rather than being cut off by it.\n\n## Testing\n\n`npx vitest run` in `modules/masonry`: **739 passed** (49 files). Six new tests on the slot, plus two existing palette tests updated because the `title` they asserted is what this replaces.\n\n| Test | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| shows the brick tooltip only after the hover delay | nothing at `delay - 1 ms`, tooltip at `delay` |\n| cancels a pending tooltip when the pointer leaves first | timer cleared on `pointerleave` |\n| keeps the tooltip out of a drag, and takes down one already showing | `pointerdown` closes it; a held pointer keeps it closed |\n| shows the tooltip on keyboard focus | focus opens, blur closes |\n| falls back to the entry's description | empty `tooltipText` |\n| renders the tooltip outside the slot | guards the clipping and `getBBox` regressions above |\n\nChecked in a browser against a throwaway Vite harness that renders palette slots inside a narrow scrolling panel, since the playground and Storybook both fail to start on `develop` (`playground/App.tsx` imports `./pages/Workspace/index`, which does not exist, and `@/index.css` does not resolve). The harness is not part of this PR. ESLint and Prettier are clean on every touched file, and `tsc --noEmit` reports the same 96 pre-existing errors as `develop`, none in these files.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added accessible, delayed tooltips for palette bricks.\n  - Tooltips appear on hover or keyboard focus and use custom text, falling back to the brick description.\n  - Tooltips remain visible without being clipped and reposition themselves near the viewport edges.\n  - Tooltips are suppressed while dragging.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
